.TH "nvme_init_manage_export_nvms_send_delete" 9 "nvme_init_manage_export_nvms_send_delete" "October 2026" "libnvme API manual" LINUX
.SH NAME
nvme_init_manage_export_nvms_send_delete \- Initialize passthru command for Manage Exported NVM Subsystem Send - Delete
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B "void" nvme_init_manage_export_nvms_send_delete
.BI "(struct libnvme_passthru_cmd *cmd "  ","
.BI "bool esubidv "  ","
.BI "__u16 esubid "  ","
.BI "struct nvme_exported_nvm_subsys_nqn_data *data "  ");"
.SH ARGUMENTS
.IP "cmd" 12
Passthru command to use
.IP "esubidv" 12
Exported NVM Subsystem Identifier Valid (ESUBIDV): if set,
\fIesubid\fP identifies the Exported NVM Subsystem to delete;
otherwise it is identified by the SUBNQN in \fIdata\fP
.IP "esubid" 12
Exported NVM Subsystem Identifier (ESUBID), used if
\fIesubidv\fP is set
.IP "data" 12
Exported NVM Subsystem NQN data buffer, see \fIstruct
nvme_exported_nvm_subsys_nqn_data\fP. Ignored if \fIesubidv\fP is set.
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Initializes the passthru command buffer for the Manage Exported NVM
Subsystem Send command with SEL value
NVME_MANAGE_EXPORT_NVMS_SEND_SEL_DELETE.
